  "summary": "This vibrant <b>Greek orzo bowl</b> brings Mediterranean Mediterranean flavors to your dinner table using a single convenient cooking pot for quick preparation and easy cleanup. Uncooked orzo pasta is briefly toasted in olive oil alongside diced red onions and garlic, unlocking a subtle nutty aroma before simmered directly in seasoned broth and tomatoes. As the pasta absorbs the savory liquid, it releases starches that naturally thicken the dish into a luscious, risotto-like consistency without requiring cream. Sliced kalamata olives bring a pleasantly salty kick that complements the sweet notes of canned ripe tomatoes and dried oregano. Tender baby spinach is folded into the hot pot at the very end, wilting instantly while maintaining its bright green color and fresh taste. A generous squeeze of fresh lemon juice brightens the overall profile, while creamy crumbled feta cheese melts slightly over the warm pasta, binding all the ingredients together. Enjoy this satisfying meal served hot straight from the pot into wide rimmed bowls for a complete Mediterranean dinner.",
